            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Populus suaveolens, called the Mongolian poplar, Korean poplar and Japanese poplar, is a species of flowering plant in the genus Populus, native to all of northern Asia, the Korean peninsula, the Kurils, and northern Japan. It is a tree reaching {{Convert abbreviated|30|m}}."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Forms\nThe following form is currently accepted:\nPopulus suaveolens f. baicalensis (Kom.) I.V.Belyaeva & Kovt."
